<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Melchior Ndadaye</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1953–1993</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Melchior Ndadaye was the first democratically elected president of Burundi and its first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a> head of state. Leader of the FRODEBU party, he won the election of June 1993 and took office in July. He was killed in a coup attempt by Tutsi army officers on 21 October 1993, and the massacres that followed began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burundian-civil-war">Burundian Civil War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/melchior-ndadaye.jpg" alt="Melchior Ndadaye" width="320" height="391" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RTNB (Burundi National Radio and Television) · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Melchior_Ndadaye_speaking_to_RTNB_at_Bujumbura_airport.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
